# ViRent domain conventions

## Category / dynamic attributes
No hardcoded "type" enum. Instead:
- categories: id, name, slug, icon, sort_order
- category_attributes: category_id, key, label, field_type (text/number/select/boolean), options(json), required, sort_order
- vehicles.specs (json) — populated based on the category's attributes

## Pricing
All logic lives in `PricingService`, NEVER in a controller or model.
- vehicle_rates: vehicle_id, rate_type(daily/weekly/monthly), price
- Tier breakdown: monthly_rate + duration≥28 days → full months + daily remainder; weekly_rate + duration≥7 days → full weeks + daily remainder; otherwise daily×days
- Extra prices are snapshotted in booking_extras

## Booking conflicts
- `lockForUpdate()` at confirmation time
- Per-category `buffer_hours` factored into conflict checks
- maintenance_blocks also count as "booked" periods

## Real-time hold (Reverb)
- 10-minute hold during checkout
- Cancellation/expiry → immediate release + `VehicleAvailabilityChanged` broadcast

## Rental with/without operator
- vehicles.available_with_operator (bool) + operator_daily_rate (nullable) — relevant only for machinery categories

## Auth & roles
Single `users` table for both staff and customers — no separate guard/model.
- users.role enum: admin, staff, customer
- User implements canAccessPanel() — only admin/staff pass
- customers table holds rental-specific profile (license, company info), 1:1 via user_id, customer-role users only
- bookings.customer_id references customers, not users directly

## Future: staff vs admin permission split
`staff` role currently has identical Filament panel access to `admin` (no
distinction in canAccessPanel() or resource policies). Planned future work:
Filament Policies to restrict staff from sensitive actions (deleting vehicles,
managing other staff/admin users, Stripe/financial settings). Not implemented yet.